        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add account feed model API",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Adds the first live ClawHub account/publisher feed projection for active public users, publishers, skills, and plugin packages.\r\n- Adds `/api/v1/accounts/{accountId}`, `/api/v1/accounts/{accountId}/feed`, `/api/v1/publishers/{publisherId}`, and `/api/v1/publishers/{publisherId}/feed` HTTP routes with bounded read limits and public cache headers for feed responses.\r\n- Adds the reusable `clawhub-schema` account-feed contract, OpenAPI docs, focused handler/schema/projection tests, and keeps `specs/account-feeds.md` aligned with the implemented first slice.\r\n\r\n## Trust boundary\r\n\r\nThis PR intentionally does not add official state, follow state, registry review state, scan authority, install authority, feed signing, trust roots, or cursor pagination. Feed bodies are public discovery projections only. Cursor input is ignored in this first slice, `nextCursor` is always `null`, IDs are normalized to the expected Convex table before reads, skill-family package rows are excluded from plugin feed entries, source scans are bounded while continuing past filtered rows within the scan window, already-decoded route path segments are not decoded a second time, and malformed percent-encoded route paths return normal 404s instead of server errors.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n- `git diff --cached --check`\r\n- `npx --yes oxfmt@0.56.0 --check convex/accountFeeds.ts convex/accountFeeds.test.ts convex/httpApiV1/accountFeedsV1.ts convex/httpApiV1.accountFeeds.test.ts specs/account-feeds.md`\r\n- `npx --yes oxfmt --check convex/accountFeeds.test.ts`\r\n- `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('public/api/v1/openapi.json','utf8')); console.log('openapi json ok')\"`\r\n- `node --check packages/schema/dist/accountFeed.js`\r\n- `codex review --base origin/main` reported no discrete actionable regressions.\r\n- CI repair on `9446b053`: fixed the projection test mock so the filtered-package pagination regression reuses one package query instance and advances to the older public row instead of resetting to the first filtered page.\r\n- `bun --version` was not run successfully: `bun` is not installed in this Windows shell.\r\n- Targeted Vitest/tsc/Convex codegen were not run locally because this checkout has no `node_modules` and no local `vitest`, `tsc`, or `convex` binaries.\r\n\r\n",
